WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }
::cue(c.credits) { color: #a8c7fa; font-size: 78%; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:03.370
Get running, get running

3
00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:06.460
holding our flag high in the sky

4
00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:18.060
Cross this endless sea with me and search for

5
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:21.810
a global miracle no one

6
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.940
has yet been able to find

7
00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:27.960
With our hearts pounding,

8
00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.710
we'll just charge ahead as we please, following

9
00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:35.590
the footprints of those who pursue their dreams

10
00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:39.390
No matter how stormy the night,

11
00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:42.390
if we put our minds together,

12
00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:46.540
we'll get through it

13
00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:47.860
always

14
00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:51.590
Get running, get running

15
00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:54.550
holding our flag high in the sky

16
00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:57.140
Even though there are tears

17
00:00:57.230 --> 00:01:00.580
we don't want anyone to see

18
00:01:00.770 --> 00:01:03.520
Keep chasing, keep chasing

19
00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:06.520
the compass that leads to our dreams

20
00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:09.230
always points straight ahead

21
00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:11.400
We can't stop here

22
00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:21.490
Get running, get running,

23
00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:24.540
head past everyone else

24
00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:27.120
So long as we don't run from it,

25
00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:30.540
we can take hold of tomorrow

26
00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:33.630
Keep chasing, keep chasing

27
00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:36.510
everything we see in the moment,

28
00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:38.930
we should record it all

29
00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:41.430
in the blank slates of our minds

30
00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:57.170
<b>The Terrifying Emergency Broadcast</b>

31
00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:54.580
I'm impressed. I'll give you that much.

32
00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:59.050
It's hard to believe that you've come this far... all by yourself.

33
00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:03.610
There's no way I could come this far by myself,

34
00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:05.760
and I wouldn't even wanna come by myself.

35
00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:11.690
Unlike you guys, I don't work alone!

36
00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:15.580
Soon all my friends will be here!

37
00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:28.910
Tempest Kick!

38
00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:38.540
Shave!

39
00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:40.530
Th-Th-That was close!

40
00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:41.650
Don't let your guard down!

41
00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:43.010
O-Okay.

42
00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:44.850
And don't do anything stupid!

43
00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:46.560
O-Okay.

44
00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:49.310
Hm?! What's that supposed
to mean?! How insulting!

45
00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:51.060
You're so damn rude!

46
00:02:56.690 --> 00:03:00.500
Oh no! It's so slippery that I can't stand.

47
00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:01.860
Even still,

48
00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:06.680
just you wait. I'm about to get you back!

49
00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:18.050
Ow, ow, ow. That damn deer-gorilla!
How dare he humiliate me?!

50
00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:22.100
But the key is more important! We gotta get the key!

51
00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.720
I'd better hurry to that secretary woman.

52
00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:35.110
Deer-gorilla! Wait, you jerk!

53
00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:00.720
Let's go, Oimo!

54
00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:02.680
Yeah, Kashi!

55
00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:07.270
We've got to try and take them out one at a time!

56
00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:10.350
Artillery squad! Concentrate
your fire on Kashi's feet!

57
00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:19.320
Now! Charge!

58
00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.940
Has the situation outside changed?

59
00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:33.290
The giants who changed sides have been doing all they can to defend us,

60
00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:35.600
but I guess they're at the end of their rope.

61
00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:57.880
Hey! Hey, hurry up!

62
00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:01.940
Dammit! What a disaster.

63
00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:04.970
I can't believe a pirate could get this far.

64
00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:08.630
Hey, everyone, come in!

65
00:05:08.630 --> 00:05:11.660
CP9! What the hell are you all doing?!

66
00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:14.220
A pirate has made it nearly to the bridge!

67
00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:19.040
Hey, are you listening?! Say something!

68
00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:26.370
Wait!

69
00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:30.510
You're holding...

70
00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:38.900
Whaaat?!

71
00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:44.920
The... The... The golden transponder snail!

72
00:05:55.700 --> 00:06:09.300
Navy

73
00:05:56.900 --> 00:06:00.060
The silver transponder snail
has received a signal!

74
00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:02.330
A buster call has been sounded!

75
00:06:02.330 --> 00:06:06.010
Admiral Aokiji has sounded a buster call!

76
00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:07.350
Where?

77
00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:09.300
Enies Lobby!

78
00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:12.760
Have the five vice admirals closest to the target respond!

79
00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:14.200
Considering the distance,

80
00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:15.970
I think it's quicker to head
there from headquarters.

81
00:06:15.970 --> 00:06:17.460
How long will it take?

82
00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:19.900
It's possible to get there within 30 minutes.

83
00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:22.870
Immediately have ten battleships
get ready to set sail,

84
00:06:22.870 --> 00:06:24.830
and summon five vice admirals!

85
00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:26.060
Double time!

86
00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:27.440
Yes, sir!

87
00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:29.690
A buster call has been sounded!

88
00:06:29.690 --> 00:06:32.070
The target is Enies Lobby!

89
00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:35.410
Have ten battleships get
ready to set sail immediately!

90
00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:37.570
Hey! Hey!

91
00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:39.550
Yes, Chief.

92
00:06:39.550 --> 00:06:42.640
Dammit! Oh, crap! This one is
the mobile transponder snail.

93
00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:44.750
What have I done? I wasn't careful.

94
00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:48.720
How did I press the button
on the golden transponder snail?!

95
00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:51.340
How could I have...

96
00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:56.120
sounded a buster call?!

97
00:07:07.830 --> 00:07:10.440
A-a buster call? I-It can't be!

98
00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:12.160
What's this? Some announcement?

99
00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:16.200
How could you do something so stupid?! Rescind the order immediately!

100
00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:18.660
That's Robin's voice!

101
00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:21.120
It'll be a disaster!

102
00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:23.080
Robin!

103
00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:26.480
What? "Rescind the order"?

104
00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:30.920
Hey, hey. Who do you think you're talking to?

105
00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:33.050
What the heck is this broadcast?

106
00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:34.390
Hey! Don't move!

107
00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:36.430
We can't move!

108
00:07:42.860 --> 00:07:47.220
A buster call is a great idea!
What's wrong with it?!

109
00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:51.030
That's Chief Spandam's voice, right?

110
00:07:56.480 --> 00:07:59.900
That's right. There's no problem.

111
00:07:59.900 --> 00:08:04.380
I'm the chief of Cipher Pol No. 9.

112
00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:07.330
To facilitate handing you over to the government,

113
00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:09.490
I sounded a buster call.

114
00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:12.470
I see no problem in that!

115
00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:15.460
Even in the worst-case scenario,

116
00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:20.600
we'll be sure to put an end to those pirates.

117
00:08:21.670 --> 00:08:23.370
How could you be so absurd?!

118
00:08:23.370 --> 00:08:26.610
I thought I told you!
That won't be the end of it!

119
00:08:27.090 --> 00:08:30.310
There's no humanity in that attack!

120
00:08:31.380 --> 00:08:35.200
That's the chief, but who's the woman?

121
00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:38.980
The attack will burn
Enies Lobby to the ground!

122
00:08:38.980 --> 00:08:42.250
Buildings, people... the very island itself!

123
00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:50.200
It's a nightmarish concentration of fire that
sacrifices everything to achieve its goal!

124
00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:52.260
That's the buster call!

125
00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:57.890
You have no idea what happened on Ohara twenty years ago!

126
00:08:58.590 --> 00:09:04.810
That's fine. It means that this is
very important to the government.

127
00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:09.520
Now that that idiot Cutty Flam has
burned the blueprints for Pluton,

128
00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:26.530
your existence is the only
clue to the ancient weapon.

129
00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:31.310
A military power that can turn this
whole era upside down is at stake.

130
00:09:31.310 --> 00:09:37.760
If it improves our chances of killing
those idiots trying to get you back,

131
00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:41.600
even if it causes the death
of thousands of soldiers,

132
00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:46.060
we can say that it's an unavoidable
sacrifice for our glorious future!

133
00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:51.020
Above all of that, my promotion is at stake, too.

134
00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:53.550
What?! What's he saying?!

135
00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:56.530
He's gonna sacrifice us?! You gotta be kidding!

136
00:09:56.530 --> 00:09:59.450
What do you think of people's lives?!

137
00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:04.380
Don't forget that CP9 is the
government's secret organization.

138
00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:09.270
If we need 100 deaths in
order to save 1,000 lives,

139
00:10:09.270 --> 00:10:13.460
we won't hesitate to take those 100 lives on the spot.

140
00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:23.310
Mercilessness is also
a necessity for true justice.

141
00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:30.810
Besides, those incompetent soldiers
who couldn't stop the invading pirates...

142
00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:33.490
are better off dead, you idiot!

143
00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:41.430
That mobile transponder snail is transmitting.

144
00:10:41.430 --> 00:10:43.200
What?

145
00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:45.660
Ahhh! Shoot!

146
00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:48.160
Did everyone hear what I just said?!

147
00:10:53.470 --> 00:10:58.510
S-So... my name is Straw Hat Luffy.

148
00:10:58.510 --> 00:11:00.130
You liar!

149
00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:02.540
Everyone! Leave the island!

150
00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:05.100
Enies Lobby is the target of a buster call!

151
00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:08.020
If you stay on the island, you won't survive!

152
00:11:08.020 --> 00:11:11.480
This isn't your concern!

153
00:11:20.290 --> 00:11:22.410
– A b-...
– A buster call...

154
00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:27.410
It sounds like a buster call has been sounded.

155
00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:30.370
What the hell is that man doing?

156
00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:32.480
Sounds like there's some sort of danger.

157
00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:34.630
It's me who's in danger!

158
00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:37.670
I feel sorry for you guys.

159
00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:40.420
Now you have no hope.

160
00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:42.250
Don't worry.

161
00:11:42.250 --> 00:11:45.890
We're used to situations like this.

162
00:11:49.150 --> 00:11:54.860
Pirate kid, what kind of
star were you born under?

163
00:11:55.160 --> 00:11:59.400
This is getting even more interesting!

164
00:12:02.300 --> 00:12:04.510
A buster call has been sounded!

165
00:12:04.510 --> 00:12:06.220
Battleships are coming!

166
00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:10.370
Get off of Enies Lobby!

167
00:12:12.990 --> 00:12:16.020
Battleships are coming? Why are
the Navy soldiers running away?

168
00:12:16.020 --> 00:12:18.450
The woman said that the island
will be burned to the ground.

169
00:12:18.450 --> 00:12:20.210
But this is the government's island!

170
00:12:20.210 --> 00:12:22.090
How should I know why?!

171
00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:26.260
Hey, hey! If you guys are running away,
at least untie us first!

172
00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:34.310
It's a buster call!

173
00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:36.450
We'll be dead if we stay here!

174
00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:39.460
Bring some ships to the front!
Get ready to sail!

175
00:12:39.460 --> 00:12:42.990
The Navy is coming to attack!

176
00:12:47.440 --> 00:12:49.350
We got left behind.

177
00:12:49.350 --> 00:12:52.970
Hey! What're we gonna do?!
Isn't this dangerous?!

178
00:12:52.970 --> 00:12:56.260
It's been dangerous ever since
we set foot in this place.

179
00:12:56.260 --> 00:12:59.750
What about our bro?! What's gonna
happen to Big Bro Franky?!

180
00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:03.780
Yeah. If he doesn't make it back here,
we can't go home together!

181
00:13:03.780 --> 00:13:05.430
The Straw Hats, too!

182
00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:08.180
So what about us?!

183
00:13:09.270 --> 00:13:14.140
What will... happen to all of us?!

184
00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:17.400
We can't afford to waste time, either.

185
00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:20.980
Yeah, we have to take them out quickly
and hurry to the Gates of Justice.

186
00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:22.690
I've got an idea.

187
00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:25.770
Wh-What? What idea?

188
00:13:25.770 --> 00:13:29.440
A way to get the handcuffs off?
Or a way to escape from here?

189
00:13:29.440 --> 00:13:33.790
You are the named blade Nose Storm.

190
00:13:33.790 --> 00:13:36.720
This is no time to give me a nice name!

191
00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:40.290
Chopper! What's taking so long?!

192
00:13:51.410 --> 00:13:54.270
How dare you open your mouth
and say something so stupid?!

193
00:13:55.130 --> 00:13:58.150
If the pirates really get away,

194
00:13:59.090 --> 00:14:00.920
how are you going to...

195
00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:05.650
take responsibility for it?!

196
00:14:10.720 --> 00:14:12.410
What was that?!

197
00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:15.580
Where was Robin speaking from?!

198
00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:18.350
The other side of these doors.

199
00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:29.380
I can't let you pass.
At least give me time to say that.

200
00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:19.730
Get out of my way.
Robin's behind those doors, right?!

201
00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:22.900
Yeah, she's there. So what?
You won't be able to see her...

202
00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:25.270
ever again.

203
00:15:28.940 --> 00:15:31.350
The pressure sure has suddenly ramped up.

204
00:15:34.260 --> 00:15:38.160
Sounds like if I stay in this tower for too long, I may die.

205
00:15:40.470 --> 00:15:43.520
If you're gonna run, then leave the key here.

206
00:15:43.520 --> 00:15:44.210
Shave!

207
00:15:44.680 --> 00:15:46.160
I'm sorry.

208
00:15:47.430 --> 00:15:50.590
I wanted to spend more time playing with you.

209
00:15:57.180 --> 00:15:58.550
Shoot!

210
00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:12.700
We have to quickly evacuate, too.

211
00:16:20.240 --> 00:16:21.910
Golden Bubbles!

212
00:16:32.650 --> 00:16:36.260
This is the same attack that got Sanji-kun.
I thought I was being careful.

213
00:16:43.160 --> 00:16:45.180
I can't hold my Clima-Tact.

214
00:16:47.010 --> 00:16:50.110
My entire body is slippery! I can't stand up!

215
00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:56.670
How dare you make my body like this?!

216
00:16:57.660 --> 00:17:01.980
Although it has the downside
of reducing your curves,

217
00:17:01.980 --> 00:17:04.710
it does give you the most beautiful skin.

218
00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:06.420
I envy you.

219
00:17:06.970 --> 00:17:10.010
But in return, your fighting
ability is reduced by half.

220
00:17:10.010 --> 00:17:12.920
You should just give up on the key I have.

221
00:17:13.220 --> 00:17:16.430
I... I can't do that!

222
00:17:16.430 --> 00:17:18.200
Cool Charge!

223
00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:24.630
That's no use. Playtime is over.

224
00:17:25.440 --> 00:17:26.240
Tempest Kick!

225
00:17:28.550 --> 00:17:29.550
What?

226
00:17:30.210 --> 00:17:31.780
Mirage Tempo.

227
00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:33.480
I'm right here.

228
00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:36.110
When did you...?! What's going on?

229
00:17:36.110 --> 00:17:36.910
Finger Pistol!

230
00:17:42.690 --> 00:17:45.490
Another fake! Where are you this time?!

231
00:17:45.490 --> 00:17:46.670
This way! Right here!

232
00:17:52.780 --> 00:17:54.010
What's that?!

233
00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:56.800
Sh-She became huge?!

234
00:17:56.800 --> 00:17:57.680
What?

235
00:18:00.080 --> 00:18:02.900
So you have powers, too?

236
00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:05.180
She's a ditz.

237
00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:51.260
Robin!

238
00:19:59.670 --> 00:20:01.290
It's a buster call!

239
00:20:01.290 --> 00:20:03.090
Battleships are coming!

240
00:20:03.090 --> 00:20:06.970
Hurry, or we'll be burned to a crisp!

241
00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:09.100
Get out of here!

242
00:20:16.730 --> 00:20:20.280
Zoan type? So is that your trump card?!

243
00:20:20.280 --> 00:20:23.380
Seriously, that's not me!

244
00:20:23.380 --> 00:20:25.820
At the same time, that thing...

245
00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:32.040
It looks like a reindeer, and I know that
hat and the mark on it without a doubt.

246
00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:34.270
But I can't believe...

247
00:20:34.270 --> 00:20:36.500
this is Chopper!

248
00:20:39.240 --> 00:20:41.010
What savage beast's power does she hold?!

249
00:20:43.510 --> 00:20:44.720
Moon Walk!

250
00:20:47.140 --> 00:20:48.310
Tempest Kick!

251
00:20:48.310 --> 00:20:50.500
Hey! Stop it!

252
00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:51.350
What?!

253
00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:54.420
Chopper! Hey, you're Chopper, right?

254
00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:56.480
How did you become like that?!

255
00:21:05.790 --> 00:21:08.990
I guess he can't recognize me
since I look like this.

256
00:21:08.990 --> 00:21:10.540
Aren't you Chopper?!

257
00:21:11.480 --> 00:21:12.930
Let me tell you something!

258
00:21:12.930 --> 00:21:16.830
I didn't think that was you!

259
00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:18.710
Chopper!

260
00:21:19.200 --> 00:21:22.210
Sh-She ignored me! How insolent!

261
00:21:24.420 --> 00:21:26.520
Chopper! What's wrong?!

262
00:21:26.520 --> 00:21:29.550
Take a good look at me! It's me! I'm Nami!

263
00:21:37.340 --> 00:21:38.320
Chopper!

264
00:21:43.200 --> 00:21:44.360
Chopper! Stop it!

265
00:22:01.320 --> 00:22:03.710
Sanji-kun is downstairs!

266
00:22:03.710 --> 00:22:07.330
Where did such a monster stray in here from?

267
00:22:07.330 --> 00:22:10.550
Don't hurt him! He's my friend!

268
00:22:34.440 --> 00:22:36.410
What happened to Chopper?

269
00:22:38.140 --> 00:22:40.790
This is terrible. I have to stop him right away.

270
00:22:43.770 --> 00:22:48.820
That's your friend? You pirates
sure own a creepy pet, huh?

271
00:22:48.820 --> 00:22:50.260
Chopper!

272
00:22:52.530 --> 00:22:55.640
She ignored me again! How insolent!

273
00:22:56.090 --> 00:22:58.820
You're free to go stop that monster,

274
00:22:58.820 --> 00:23:02.400
but I have a duty to stop you, too.

275
00:23:02.400 --> 00:23:05.190
I'm gonna hurry up and finish it here.

276
00:23:05.190 --> 00:23:06.140
Tempest Kick!

277
00:23:06.780 --> 00:23:11.240
This is bad! Even the soles
are slippery. I can't dodge it!

278
00:23:14.200 --> 00:23:16.060
Huh?! I dodged it!

279
00:23:16.060 --> 00:23:18.690
Ah... My right leg returned to normal.

280
00:23:18.690 --> 00:23:22.040
Why? What caused it?

281
00:23:23.100 --> 00:23:24.300
It's wet.

282
00:23:24.300 --> 00:23:27.380
It got wet in all that commotion. Oh, that's right!

283
00:23:28.380 --> 00:23:33.180
Water! I can wash off
the soap power with water!

284
00:23:46.190 --> 00:23:48.110
Aren't you being too optimistic?

285
00:23:48.110 --> 00:23:51.740
Even if you figured out how
to undo Golden Bubbles,

286
00:23:51.740 --> 00:23:53.950
there's no way I'd let you do that.

287
00:23:57.450 --> 00:24:00.410
Sheep Cloud: Relaxing Bubbles!

288
00:24:01.650 --> 00:24:04.710
I'll blow away those bubbles with wind!

289
00:24:04.710 --> 00:24:06.060
Cyclone...

290
00:24:08.360 --> 00:24:09.560
Shoot!

291
00:24:12.500 --> 00:24:16.050
O... Oh, no... My strength is...

292
00:24:19.310 --> 00:24:20.520
Elastic Finger Pistol...

293
00:24:21.490 --> 00:24:22.730
Tact...

294
00:24:22.730 --> 00:24:24.080
Whip!

295
00:24:40.130 --> 00:24:41.770
That was helpful.

296
00:24:41.770 --> 00:24:43.120
Helpful?

297
00:24:45.220 --> 00:24:48.770
If you toss me around like that,

298
00:24:48.770 --> 00:24:52.320
the annoying bubbles on my
body get tossed off, too.

299
00:24:52.320 --> 00:24:57.100
You're bluffing. If you so wish,
I'll keep throwing you around until you die.

300
00:25:00.590 --> 00:25:02.770
The forecast is cloudy!

301
00:25:02.770 --> 00:25:04.540
Cloudy Tempo!

302
00:25:07.840 --> 00:25:11.280
This is different from the
magic show stuff I used to do!

303
00:25:13.150 --> 00:25:15.740
Clouds? More lightning?

304
00:25:18.120 --> 00:25:21.690
Thunder doesn't get generated
from such thin clouds.

305
00:25:21.690 --> 00:25:24.790
Instead, they'll condense!

306
00:25:25.450 --> 00:25:26.300
Don't tell me!

307
00:25:26.300 --> 00:25:28.300
No, she might do it!

308
00:25:29.210 --> 00:25:31.250
The forecast is rain!

309
00:25:31.250 --> 00:25:32.340
Cool Ball!

310
00:25:32.340 --> 00:25:33.630
Shave!

311
00:25:34.590 --> 00:25:36.050
Pour down!

312
00:25:36.050 --> 00:25:37.880
Rain Tempo!

313
00:25:45.980 --> 00:25:50.230
You're not sweet at all. After I was nice
enough to make your skin silky smooth.

314
00:25:50.230 --> 00:25:55.110
If being sweet means not
putting up a fight, then I'll pass.

315
00:25:55.110 --> 00:25:56.650
Cool Charge!

316
00:26:00.530 --> 00:26:01.650
What?

317
00:26:02.540 --> 00:26:04.710
Mirage Tempo!

318
00:26:07.440 --> 00:26:08.610
She disappeared?!

319
00:26:08.610 --> 00:26:12.460
Now I understand your powers,

320
00:26:13.970 --> 00:26:16.130
as well as the strength of CP9.

321
00:26:16.130 --> 00:26:18.450
What's this?!

322
00:26:20.490 --> 00:26:22.250
Mirage Tempo:

323
00:26:23.260 --> 00:26:25.930
Fata Morgana!
